IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cbca-core-definitions`
IMPORT `cb3-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XIV -- Financial Disclosure: the auditor, the
-- audit committee and qualified privilege (ss 161 to 172). The statements (ss 155 to 160) are in
-- cb3-part14-statements.l4; Part XIV.1 (s 172.1) is in cb3-part14-1-diversity.l4.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Rules are named `<what> within s N`. A court's order is the court's
-- discretion and is never decided: a rule says who may apply, on what ground, and what power the court has.
-- "Forthwith" and "without delay" are the caller's judgment (a plain BOOLEAN). "Independence is a question of
-- fact" and "reasonableness is a question of fact" are plain BOOLEANs of the same kind. Dates carry no time of day.
-- Dates: Part XIV holds no enactment, assent or commencement provision, so no date is carried.

§ `Part XIV -- Financial Disclosure: the auditor (ss 161 to 172)`

§§ `s 161 -- qualification of the auditor`

-- (2.1) For the purposes of (2), a person's business partner "includes" a shareholder of that person. The inclusion adds to
-- the ordinary meaning, which the caller states.
-- src:1976 | (2.1) For the purposes of subsection (2), a person’s business partner includes a shareholder of that person.
@ref CBCA s 161(2.1) (src:1976)
GIVEN `the other is a business partner of the person in the ordinary sense` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other is a shareholder of the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a business partner within s 161(2.1)` MEANS
        `the other is a business partner of the person in the ordinary sense`
    OR  `the other is a shareholder of the person`

-- (2)(b) A person is deemed not independent if they or their business partner (i) is a business partner, a director, an officer
-- or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any
-- such corporation or its affiliates; (ii) beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the
-- securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates; or (iii) has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator
-- or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates within two years of the person's proposed appointment as
-- auditor. For (iii) the caller gives the last day the person or partner held such an office (NOTHING if never); the appointment is
-- within two years if it is on or before the last day of two years counted from that day.
-- src:1971 | (b) a person is deemed not to be independent if they or their business partner
-- src:1972 | (i) is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or any of its affiliates,
-- src:1973 | (ii) beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or
-- src:1974 | (iii) has been a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates within two years of the person’s proposed appointment as auditor of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 161(2)(b) (src:1971-1974)
`the two years of s 161(2)(b)(iii)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 2, `unit of time` IS `calendar years`

@ref CBCA s 161(2)(b) (src:1971-1974)
GIVEN `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the last day the person or their business partner was a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates, if ever` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date of the person's proposed appointment as auditor of the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is deemed not independent within s 161(2)(b)` MEANS
        `the person or their business partner is a business partner, a director, an officer or an employee of the corporation or any of its affiliates, or a business partner of any director, officer or employee of any such corporation or its affiliates`
    OR  `the person or their business partner beneficially owns or controls, directly or indirectly, a material interest in the securities of the corporation or any of its affiliates`
    OR  (CONSIDER `the last day the person or their business partner was a receiver, receiver-manager, sequestrator, liquidator or trustee in bankruptcy of the corporation or any of its affiliates, if ever`
         WHEN JUST lastDay THEN `the date of the person's proposed appointment as auditor of the corporation` AT MOST (`the last day of` `the two years of s 161(2)(b)(iii)` `counted from` lastDay)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)

-- (2)(a), (1) Independence is a question of fact: the caller's finding that the person is not independent, or the deeming of
-- (2)(b), makes the person not independent. A person who is not independent is disqualified, subject to (5).
-- src:1967 | 161 (1) Subject to subsection (5), a person is disqualified from being an auditor of a corporation if the person is not independent of the corporation, any of its affiliates, or the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates.
-- src:1968 | Independence
-- src:1969 | (2) For the purposes of this section,
-- src:1970 | (a) independence is a question of fact; and
-- src:1971 | (b) a person is deemed not to be independent if they or their business partner
@ref CBCA s 161(1), (2)(a) (src:1967 src:1970)
GIVEN `the person is independent of the corporation, its affiliates, and the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates, as a question of fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is deemed not independent under paragraph 161(2)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is not independent within s 161(2)` MEANS
        `the person is deemed not independent under paragraph 161(2)(b)`
    OR  (NOT `the person is independent of the corporation, its affiliates, and the directors or officers of any such corporation or its affiliates, as a question of fact`)

@ref CBCA s 161(1) (src:1967)
GIVEN `the person is not independent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an exemption order has been made under subsection 161(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person is disqualified from being an auditor within s 161(1)` MEANS
        `the person is not independent`
    AND (NOT `an exemption order has been made under subsection 161(5)`)

-- (3) An auditor who becomes disqualified shall, subject to (5), resign forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification.
-- The relation: the shareholders are owed the resignation; the auditor owes it.
-- src:1978 | (3) An auditor who becomes disqualified under this section shall, subject to subsection (5), resign forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification.
@ref CBCA s 161(3) (src:1978)
GIVEN `the auditor is disqualified under section 161` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor must resign forthwith within s 161(3)` MEANS
    `the auditor is disqualified under section 161`

@ref CBCA s 161(3) (src:1978)
GIVEN `the auditor must resign forthwith within s 161(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor resigned forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to resign is met within s 161(3)` MEANS
        (NOT `the auditor must resign forthwith within s 161(3)`)
    OR  `the auditor resigned forthwith after becoming aware of the disqualification`

-- (4) An interested person may apply to a court for an order declaring an auditor disqualified and the office vacant.
-- src:1980 | (4) An interested person may apply to a court for an order declaring an auditor to be disqualified under this section and the office of auditor to be vacant.
@ref CBCA s 161(4) (src:1980)
GIVEN `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is disqualified under section 161` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an interested person may apply for a disqualification order within s 161(4)` MEANS
        `the applicant is an interested person`
    AND `the auditor is disqualified under section 161`

-- (5) An interested person may apply to a court for an order exempting an auditor from disqualification; the court may, if
-- satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders, make an exemption order on such terms as it thinks fit,
-- which may have retrospective effect. Who may apply, and the one ground on which the power arises, are decided; the terms are the court's.
-- src:1982 | (5) An interested person may apply to a court for an order exempting an auditor from disqualification under this section and the court may, if it is satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders, make an exemption order on such terms as it thinks fit, which order may have retrospective effect.
@ref CBCA s 161(5) (src:1982)
GIVEN `the applicant is an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an interested person may apply for an exemption order within s 161(5)` MEANS
    `the applicant is an interested person`

@ref CBCA s 161(5) (src:1982)
GIVEN `an application for an exemption order is made by an interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may make an exemption order within s 161(5)` MEANS
        `an application for an exemption order is made by an interested person`
    AND `the court is satisfied that an exemption would not unfairly prejudice the shareholders`

@ref CBCA s 161(5) (src:1982)
GIVEN `the court has made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the exemption order may have retrospective effect within s 161(5)` MEANS
    `the court has made an exemption order under subsection 161(5)`

§§ `s 162 -- appointment of the auditor`

-- (1) Subject to s 163, the shareholders shall, by ordinary resolution, at the first annual meeting and at each succeeding annual
-- meeting, appoint an auditor to hold office until the close of the next annual meeting. The relation: the corporation and the
-- public are owed the appointment; the shareholders owe it. The ordinary resolution is the keel's (s 2(1)).
-- src:1984 | 162 (1) Subject to section 163, shareholders of a corporation shall, by ordinary resolution, at the first annual meeting of shareholders and at each succeeding annual meeting, appoint an auditor to hold office until the close of the next annual meeting.
@ref CBCA s 162(1) (src:1984)
GIVEN `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders must appoint an auditor within s 162(1)` MEANS
        `it is the first annual meeting of shareholders or a succeeding annual meeting`
    AND (NOT `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor`)

@ref CBCA s 162(1) (src:1984)
GIVEN `the shareholders must appoint an auditor within s 162(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor is appointed by ordinary resolution within s 162(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the shareholders must appoint an auditor within s 162(1)`)
    OR  `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` tally

@ref CBCA s 162(1) (src:1984)
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE
      `the date of the close of the next annual meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointed auditor holds office within s 162(1)` MEANS
    `the date` AT MOST `the date of the close of the next annual meeting`

-- (2) An auditor appointed under s 104 is eligible for appointment under (1). Eligible by this subsection; s 161 still applies.
-- src:1986 | (2) An auditor appointed under section 104 is eligible for appointment under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 162(2) (src:1986)
GIVEN `the auditor was appointed under section 104` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor appointed under section 104 is eligible within s 162(2)` MEANS
    `the auditor was appointed under section 104`

-- (3) Despite (1), if an auditor is not appointed at a meeting, the incumbent auditor continues in office until a successor is
-- appointed.
-- src:1988 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1), if an auditor is not appointed at a meeting of shareholders, the incumbent auditor continues in office until a successor is appointed.
@ref CBCA s 162(3) (src:1988)
GIVEN `an auditor is not appointed at a meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a successor has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the incumbent auditor continues in office within s 162(3)` MEANS
        `an auditor is not appointed at a meeting of shareholders`
    AND (NOT `a successor has been appointed`)

-- (4) The remuneration may be fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders or, if not so fixed, by the directors.
-- src:1990 | (4) The remuneration of an auditor may be fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders or, if not so fixed, may be fixed by the directors.
@ref CBCA s 162(4) (src:1990)
GIVEN `the remuneration has been fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors may fix the remuneration of the auditor within s 162(4)` MEANS
    (NOT `the remuneration has been fixed by ordinary resolution of the shareholders`)

§§ `s 163 -- dispensing with the auditor`

-- (1) The shareholders of a corporation that is not a distributing corporation may resolve not to appoint an auditor. (2) The
-- resolution is valid only until the next succeeding annual meeting (fork F-163-until: until the meeting, not the close of it, so
-- valid on dates before the meeting day). (3) It is not valid unless consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not
-- otherwise entitled to vote.
-- src:1992 | 163 (1) The shareholders of a corporation that is not a distributing corporation may resolve not to appoint an auditor.
-- src:1993 | Limitation
-- src:1994 | (2) A resolution under subsection (1) is valid only until the next succeeding annual meeting of shareholders.
-- src:1995 | Unanimous consent
-- src:1996 | (3) A resolution under subsection (1) is not valid unless it is consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote.
@ref CBCA s 163 (src:1992-1996)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`shareholders may resolve not to appoint an auditor within s 163(1)` MEANS
    (NOT `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)

@ref CBCA s 163 (src:1992-1996)
GIVEN `the corporation is a distributing corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resolution is consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date` IS A DATE
      `the date of the next succeeding annual meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the resolution not to appoint an auditor is valid within s 163` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation is a distributing corporation`)
    AND `the resolution is consented to by all the shareholders, including shareholders not otherwise entitled to vote`
    AND `the date` LESS THAN `the date of the next succeeding annual meeting`

§§ `s 164 -- ceasing to hold office`

-- (1) An auditor ceases to hold office when the auditor (a) dies or resigns; or (b) is removed pursuant to s 165. (2) A resignation
-- becomes effective at the time a written resignation is sent to the corporation, or at the time specified in it, whichever is later.
-- The time is a day here: the later of the two dates.
-- src:1999 | 164 (1) An auditor of a corporation ceases to hold office when the auditor
-- src:2000 | (a) dies or resigns; or
-- src:2001 | (b) is removed pursuant to section 165.
@ref CBCA s 164(1) (src:1999-2001)
GIVEN `the auditor dies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor resigns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor is removed pursuant to section 165` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor ceases to hold office within s 164(1)` MEANS
        `the auditor dies`
    OR  `the auditor resigns`
    OR  `the auditor is removed pursuant to section 165`

-- src:2003 | (2) A resignation of an auditor becomes effective at the time a written resignation is sent to the corporation, or at the time specified in the resignation, whichever is later.
@ref CBCA s 164(2) (src:2003)
GIVEN `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation` IS A DATE
      `the date specified in the resignation, if any` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the resignation becomes effective within s 164(2)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date specified in the resignation, if any`
    WHEN JUST specified THEN IF specified GREATER THAN `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation` THEN specified ELSE `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the date the written resignation is sent to the corporation`

§§ `s 165 -- removal of the auditor`

-- (1) The shareholders may by ordinary resolution at a special meeting remove the auditor, other than an auditor appointed by a
-- court under s 167. (2) A vacancy created by the removal may be filled at the meeting at which the auditor is removed or, if not
-- so filled, under s 166.
-- src:2005 | 165 (1) The shareholders of a corporation may by ordinary resolution at a special meeting remove from office the auditor other than an auditor appointed by a court under section 167.
@ref CBCA s 165(1) (src:2005)
GIVEN `the resolution is passed at a special meeting of shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      tally IS A `Vote tally`
      `the auditor was appointed by a court under section 167` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the shareholders may remove the auditor within s 165(1)` MEANS
        `the resolution is passed at a special meeting of shareholders`
    AND `ordinary resolution within s 2(1)` tally
    AND (NOT `the auditor was appointed by a court under section 167`)

-- src:2007 | (2) A vacancy created by the removal of an auditor may be filled at the meeting at which the auditor is removed or, if not so filled, may be filled under section 166.
@ref CBCA s 165(2) (src:2007)
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the filling is at the meeting at which the auditor is removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vacancy may be filled at the meeting of removal within s 165(2)` MEANS
        `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor`
    AND `the filling is at the meeting at which the auditor is removed`

@ref CBCA s 165(2) (src:2007)
GIVEN `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the vacancy was not filled at the meeting at which the auditor was removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the vacancy may be filled under section 166 within s 165(2)` MEANS
        `the vacancy was created by the removal of an auditor`
    AND `the vacancy was not filled at the meeting at which the auditor was removed`

§§ `s 166 -- filling a vacancy`

-- (1) Subject to (3), the directors shall forthwith fill a vacancy in the office of auditor. (3) The articles may provide that a
-- vacancy shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders. The relation: the corporation and the shareholders are owed the filling;
-- the directors owe it.
-- src:2009 | 166 (1) Subject to subsection (3), the directors shall forthwith fill a vacancy in the office of auditor.
@ref CBCA s 166(1) (src:2009)
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must fill the vacancy forthwith within s 166(1)` MEANS
        `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor`
    AND (NOT `the articles provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders`)

@ref CBCA s 166(1) (src:2009)
GIVEN `the directors must fill the vacancy forthwith within s 166(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors filled the vacancy forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to fill the vacancy is met within s 166(1)` MEANS
        (NOT `the directors must fill the vacancy forthwith within s 166(1)`)
    OR  `the directors filled the vacancy forthwith`

-- src:2013 | (3) The articles of a corporation may provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 166(3) (src:2013)
GIVEN `the articles of the corporation provide that a vacancy in the office of auditor shall only be filled by vote of the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the articles may so provide within s 166(3)` MEANS
    TRUE

-- (2) If there is not a quorum of directors, the directors then in office shall, within twenty-one days after a vacancy occurs,
-- call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy and, if they fail to call a meeting or if there are no directors, the
-- meeting may be called by any shareholder. The day the vacancy occurs is day 0 and the twenty-first day after it is in time (the
-- keel's convention, fork F1).
-- src:2011 | (2) If there is not a quorum of directors, the directors then in office shall, within twenty-one days after a vacancy in the office of auditor occurs, call a special meeting of shareholders to fill the vacancy and, if they fail to call a meeting or if there are no directors, the meeting may be called by any shareholder.
@ref CBCA s 166(2) (src:2011)
`the twenty-one days of s 166(2)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 21, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 166(2) (src:2011)
GIVEN `the date the vacancy occurs` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the directors in office to call the meeting within s 166(2)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the twenty-one days of s 166(2)` `counted from` `the date the vacancy occurs`

@ref CBCA s 166(2) (src:2011)
GIVEN `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is not a quorum of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors then in office must call a special meeting within s 166(2)` MEANS
        `there is a vacancy in the office of auditor`
    AND `there is not a quorum of directors`

@ref CBCA s 166(2) (src:2011)
GIVEN `there are no directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors then in office must call a special meeting under subsection 166(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the vacancy occurs` IS A DATE
      `the date the directors called the meeting, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the shareholder calls the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`any shareholder may call the meeting within s 166(2)` MEANS
        `there are no directors`
    OR  (    `the directors then in office must call a special meeting under subsection 166(2)`
         AND (NOT (CONSIDER `the date the directors called the meeting, if they did`
                   WHEN JUST called THEN `done within the time limit` `the twenty-one days of s 166(2)` `the date the vacancy occurs` called
                   WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))
         AND `the date the shareholder calls the meeting` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the directors in office to call the meeting within s 166(2)` `the date the vacancy occurs`))

-- (4) An auditor appointed to fill a vacancy holds office for the unexpired term of the predecessor: the term ends when the
-- predecessor's would have.
-- src:2015 | (4) An auditor appointed to fill a vacancy holds office for the unexpired term of the auditor’s predecessor.
@ref CBCA s 166(4) (src:2015)
GIVEN `the date the predecessor's term of office would have ended` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date the term of the auditor appointed to fill the vacancy ends within s 166(4)` MEANS
    `the date the predecessor's term of office would have ended`

§§ `s 167 -- an auditor appointed by the court`

-- (1) If a corporation does not have an auditor, the court may, on the application of a shareholder or the Director, appoint and
-- fix the remuneration of an auditor who holds office until one is appointed by the shareholders. (2) (1) does not apply if the
-- shareholders have resolved under s 163 not to appoint one.
-- src:2017 | 167 (1) If a corporation does not have an auditor, the court may, on the application of a shareholder or the Director, appoint and fix the remuneration of an auditor who holds office until an auditor is appointed by the shareholders.
-- src:2018 | Exception
-- src:2019 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor.
@ref CBCA s 167 (src:2017-2019)
GIVEN `the corporation does not have an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the court may appoint an auditor and fix the remuneration within s 167` MEANS
        `the corporation does not have an auditor`
    AND (    `the applicant is a shareholder`
         OR  `the applicant is the Director`)
    AND (NOT `the shareholders have resolved under section 163 not to appoint an auditor`)

§§ `s 168 -- the auditor at meetings; statements; replacement`

-- (1) The auditor is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of shareholders and, at the expense of the corporation, to attend
-- and be heard on matters relating to the auditor's duties.
-- src:2021 | 168 (1) The auditor of a corporation is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of shareholders and, at the expense of the corporation, to attend and be heard on matters relating to the auditor’s duties.
@ref CBCA s 168(1) (src:2021)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor is entitled to notice of and to attend and be heard at shareholders' meetings within s 168(1)` MEANS
    `the person is the auditor of the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 168(1) (src:2021)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor attends a meeting of shareholders on matters relating to the auditor's duties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation bears the expense of the auditor's attendance within s 168(1)` MEANS
        `the person is the auditor of the corporation`
    AND `the auditor attends a meeting of shareholders on matters relating to the auditor's duties`

-- (2) If a director or shareholder, whether or not entitled to vote, gives written notice not less than ten days before a meeting
-- to the auditor or a former auditor, they shall attend the meeting at the expense of the corporation and answer questions relating to
-- their duties as auditor. The meeting day is day 0 and notice on or before the tenth day before it is in time (as in s 159(1),
-- F-159-before). The relation: the director or shareholder holds the claim; the auditor or former auditor the duty.
-- src:2023 | (2) If a director or shareholder of a corporation, whether or not the shareholder is entitled to vote at the meeting, gives written notice not less than ten days before a meeting of shareholders to the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation, the auditor or former auditor shall attend the meeting at the expense of the corporation and answer questions relating to their duties as auditor.
@ref CBCA s 168(2) (src:2023)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)` MEANS
        `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation`
    AND `a director or shareholder gave written notice to the person`
    AND `the date the notice was given` AT MOST (`the date of the meeting` MINUS 10)

@ref CBCA s 168(2) (src:2023)
GIVEN `the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person attends the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person answers questions relating to their duties as auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to attend and answer questions is met within s 168(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)`)
    OR  (    `the person attends the meeting`
         AND `the person answers questions relating to their duties as auditor`)

-- (3) A director or shareholder who sends the notice shall send concurrently a copy to the corporation.
-- src:2025 | (3) A director or shareholder who sends a notice referred to in subsection (2) shall send concurrently a copy of the notice to the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 168(3) (src:2025)
GIVEN `the date the notice was sent` IS A DATE
      `the date the copy was sent to the corporation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the copy of the notice to the corporation is sent as s 168(3) requires within s 168(3)` MEANS
    `the date the copy was sent to the corporation` EQUALS `the date the notice was sent`

-- (4) An auditor or former auditor who fails without reasonable cause to comply with (2) is guilty of an offence: fine not exceeding
-- $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
-- src:2027 | (4) An auditor or former auditor of a corporation who fails without reasonable cause to comply with subsection (2) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 168(4) (src:2027)
GIVEN `the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with subsection 168(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the failure was without reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor or former auditor is guilty of an offence within s 168(4)` MEANS
        `the auditor or former auditor must attend the meeting within s 168(2)`
    AND `the person failed to comply with subsection 168(2)`
    AND `the failure was without reasonable cause`

@ref CBCA s 168(4) (src:2027)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 168(4)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- (5) The auditor is entitled to submit to the corporation a written statement giving reasons for resigning or for opposing any
-- proposed action or resolution when the auditor (a) resigns; (b) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders
-- called to remove the auditor; (c) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another
-- person is to be appointed to fill the office; or (d) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting at which a s 163 resolution
-- is to be proposed.
-- src:2029 | (5) An auditor is entitled to submit to the corporation a written statement giving reasons for resigning or for opposing any proposed action or resolution when the auditor
-- src:2030 | (a) resigns;
-- src:2031 | (b) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office;
-- src:2032 | (c) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor, whether because of the resignation or removal of the incumbent auditor or because the auditor’s term of office has expired or is about to expire; or
-- src:2033 | (d) receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed.
@ref CBCA s 168(5) (src:2029-2033)
GIVEN `the auditor resigns` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor is entitled to submit a statement within s 168(5)` MEANS
        `the auditor resigns`
    OR  `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders called for the purpose of removing the auditor from office`
    OR  `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of directors or shareholders at which another person is to be appointed to fill the office of auditor`
    OR  `the auditor receives a notice or otherwise learns of a meeting of shareholders at which a resolution referred to in section 163 is to be proposed`

-- (5.1) On a proposed replacement of an auditor, through removal or at the end of the term, (a) the corporation shall make a
-- statement on the reasons for the proposed replacement; and (b) the proposed replacement auditor may make a statement commenting on them.
-- src:2035 | (5.1) In the case of a proposed replacement of an auditor, whether through removal or at the end of the auditor’s term, the following rules apply with respect to other statements:
-- src:2036 | (a) the corporation shall make a statement on the reasons for the proposed replacement; and
-- src:2037 | (b) the proposed replacement auditor may make a statement in which he or she comments on the reasons referred to in paragraph (a).
@ref CBCA s 168(5.1) (src:2035-2037)
GIVEN `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must make a statement on the reasons for the replacement within s 168(5.1)(a)` MEANS
    `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term`

@ref CBCA s 168(5.1)(b) (src:2037)
GIVEN `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proposed replacement auditor may comment within s 168(5.1)(b)` MEANS
    `an auditor is proposed to be replaced, through removal or at the end of the auditor's term`

-- (6) The corporation shall send a copy of the statements of (5) and (5.1) without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive
-- notice of a meeting referred to in (1) and to the Director, unless the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy
-- circular required by s 150. The relation: those shareholders and the Director are owed the copy; the corporation owes it.
-- src:2039 | (6) The corporation shall send a copy of the statements referred to in subsections (5) and (5.1) without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection (1) and to the Director, unless the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150.
@ref CBCA s 168(6) (src:2039)
GIVEN `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must send a copy of the statements within s 168(6)` MEANS
        `there is a statement under subsection 168(5) or (5.1)`
    AND (NOT `the statement is included in or attached to a management proxy circular required by section 150`)

@ref CBCA s 168(6) (src:2039)
GIVEN `the corporation must send a copy of the statements within s 168(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy was sent without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection 168(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a copy was sent without delay to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to send a copy of the statements is met within s 168(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `the corporation must send a copy of the statements within s 168(6)`)
    OR  (    `a copy was sent without delay to every shareholder entitled to receive notice of a meeting referred to in subsection 168(1)`
         AND `a copy was sent without delay to the Director`)

-- (7) No person shall accept appointment or consent to be appointed as auditor to replace an auditor who has resigned, been removed
-- or whose term has expired or is about to expire until the person has requested and received from that auditor a written statement
-- of the circumstances and the reasons for the replacement. (8) Despite (7), a person otherwise qualified may accept if, within
-- fifteen days after making the request, they do not receive a reply: the request day is day 0, and the fifteenth day after it is in
-- time to reply, so the person may accept only after that last day has passed. (9) Unless (8) applies, an appointment of a person who has
-- not complied with (7) is void.
-- src:2041 | (7) No person shall accept appointment or consent to be appointed as auditor of a corporation to replace an auditor who has resigned, been removed or whose term of office has expired or is about to expire until the person has requested and received from that auditor a written statement of the circumstances and the reasons, in that auditor’s opinion, for their replacement.
-- src:2042 | Exception
-- src:2043 | (8) Notwithstanding subsection (7), a person otherwise qualified may accept appointment or consent to be appointed as auditor of a corporation if, within fifteen days after making the request referred to in that subsection, the person does not receive a reply.
-- src:2044 | Effect of non-compliance
-- src:2045 | (9) Unless subsection (8) applies, an appointment as auditor of a corporation of a person who has not complied with subsection (7) is void.
@ref CBCA s 168(7) to (9) (src:2041-2045)
`the fifteen days of s 168(8)` MEANS `Time limit` WITH `number of units` IS 15, `unit of time` IS `calendar days`

@ref CBCA s 168(8) (src:2043)
GIVEN `the date the person made the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the auditor to reply within s 168(8)` MEANS
    `the last day of` `the fifteen days of s 168(8)` `counted from` `the date the person made the request`

@ref CBCA s 168(7) to (9) (src:2041-2045)
GIVEN `the person is otherwise qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the person made the request to the auditor being replaced, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the person received the written statement, if they did` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the date the person accepts the appointment or consents to be appointed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may accept the appointment within s 168(7) and (8)` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the person made the request to the auditor being replaced, if they did`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST requested THEN
        (CONSIDER `the date the person received the written statement, if they did`
         WHEN JUST received THEN received AT MOST `the date the person accepts the appointment or consents to be appointed`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)
        OR  (    `the person is otherwise qualified`
             AND `the date the person accepts the appointment or consents to be appointed` GREATER THAN (`the last day for the auditor to reply within s 168(8)` requested)
             AND (CONSIDER `the date the person received the written statement, if they did`
                  WHEN JUST received THEN received GREATER THAN (`the last day for the auditor to reply within s 168(8)` requested)
                  WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE))

@ref CBCA s 168(9) (src:2045)
GIVEN `the person may accept the appointment under subsections 168(7) and (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the appointment is void within s 168(9)` MEANS
    (NOT `the person may accept the appointment under subsections 168(7) and (8)`)

§§ `s 169 -- the examination`

-- (1) An auditor shall make the examination that is in their opinion necessary to enable them to report in the prescribed manner on
-- the financial statements required by the Act to be placed before the shareholders, except statements, or the part of them, that
-- relate to the period of s 155(1)(a)(ii) (the preceding financial year).
-- src:2047 | 169 (1) An auditor of a corporation shall make the examination that is in their opinion necessary to enable them to report in the prescribed manner on the financial statements required by this Act to be placed before the shareholders, except such financial statements or part thereof that relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii).
@ref CBCA s 169(1) (src:2047)
GIVEN `the statements are required by this Act to be placed before the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statements or the part relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor must examine the statements within s 169(1)` MEANS
        `the statements are required by this Act to be placed before the shareholders`
    AND (NOT `the statements or the part relate to the period referred to in subparagraph 155(1)(a)(ii)`)

-- (2) Despite s 170, an auditor may reasonably rely on the report of an auditor of a body corporate or an unincorporated business
-- whose accounts are included in whole or in part in the corporation's statements. (3) Reasonableness is a question of fact. (4) (2)
-- applies whether or not the holding corporation's statements are in consolidated form: no input on consolidation, which is the point.
-- src:2049 | (2) Notwithstanding section 170, an auditor of a corporation may reasonably rely on the report of an auditor of a body corporate or an unincorporated business the accounts of which are included in whole or in part in the financial statements of the corporation.
-- src:2050 | Reasonableness
-- src:2051 | (3) For the purpose of subsection (2), reasonableness is a question of fact.
-- src:2052 | Application
-- src:2053 | (4) Subsection (2) applies whether or not the financial statements of the holding corporation reported on by the auditor are in consolidated form.
@ref CBCA s 169(2) to (4) (src:2049-2053)
GIVEN `the accounts of a body corporate or an unincorporated business are included in whole or in part in the financial statements of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reliance on the report of its auditor is reasonable, as a question of fact` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an auditor may rely on the report of another auditor within s 169(2)` MEANS
        `the accounts of a body corporate or an unincorporated business are included in whole or in part in the financial statements of the corporation`
    AND `the reliance on the report of its auditor is reasonable, as a question of fact`

§§ `s 170 -- the right to information`

-- (1) On the demand of the auditor, the present or former directors, officers, employees, agents or mandataries of the corporation
-- shall provide any (a) information and explanations and (b) access to records, documents, books, accounts and vouchers of the
-- corporation or any of its subsidiaries that are, in the auditor's opinion, necessary for the examination and report under s 169 and
-- that they are reasonably able to provide. The relation: the auditor holds the claim; those persons the duty.
-- src:2055 | 170 (1) On the demand of an auditor of a corporation, the present or former directors, officers, employees, agents or mandataries of the corporation shall provide any
-- src:2056 | (a) information and explanations, and
-- src:2057 | (b) access to records, documents, books, accounts and vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries
-- src:2058 | that are, in the opinion of the auditor, necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169 and that the directors, officers, employees, agents or mandataries are reasonably able to provide.
@ref CBCA s 170(1) (src:2055-2058)
GIVEN `the auditor demands it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a present or former director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is information, an explanation, or access to records, documents, books, accounts or vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the auditor it is necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably able to provide it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must provide it on the auditor's demand within s 170(1)` MEANS
        `the auditor demands it`
    AND `the person is a present or former director, officer, employee, agent or mandatary of the corporation`
    AND `it is information, an explanation, or access to records, documents, books, accounts or vouchers of the corporation or any of its subsidiaries`
    AND `in the opinion of the auditor it is necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169`
    AND `the person is reasonably able to provide it`

-- (2) On the demand of the auditor, the directors shall (a) obtain from the present or former directors, officers, employees and
-- agents or mandataries of any subsidiary the information and explanations they are reasonably able to provide and that are, in the
-- auditor's opinion, necessary; and (b) furnish them to the auditor.
-- src:2060 | (2) On the demand of the auditor of a corporation, the directors of the corporation shall
-- src:2061 | (a) obtain from the present or former directors, officers, employees and agents or mandataries of any subsidiary of the corporation the information and explanations that the present or former directors, officers, employees and agents or mandataries are reasonably able to provide and that are, in the opinion of the auditor, necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169; and
-- src:2062 | (b) furnish the auditor with the information and explanations so obtained.
@ref CBCA s 170(2) (src:2060-2062)
GIVEN `the auditor demands it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must obtain and furnish the information within s 170(2)` MEANS
        `the auditor demands it`
    AND `the information and explanations are those the present or former directors, officers, employees or agents or mandataries of a subsidiary are reasonably able to provide`
    AND `in the opinion of the auditor they are necessary to enable the auditor to make the examination and report required under section 169`

@ref CBCA s 170(2) (src:2060-2062)
GIVEN `the directors must obtain and furnish the information within s 170(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors obtained the information and explanations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors furnished them to the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to obtain and furnish the information is met within s 170(2)` MEANS
        (NOT `the directors must obtain and furnish the information within s 170(2)`)
    OR  (    `the directors obtained the information and explanations`
         AND `the directors furnished them to the auditor`)

-- (3) A person who in good faith makes an oral or written communication under (1) or (2) is not liable in any civil proceeding
-- arising from having made it. The relation: the communicator holds the immunity; whoever would sue is under a disability.
-- src:2064 | (3) A person who in good faith makes an oral or written communication under subsection (1) or (2) is not liable in any civil proceeding arising from having made the communication.
@ref CBCA s 170(3) (src:2064)
GIVEN `the communication is made in good faith under subsection 170(1) or (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the proceeding is a civil proceeding arising from having made the communication` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is not liable in the civil proceeding within s 170(3)` MEANS
        `the communication is made in good faith under subsection 170(1) or (2)`
    AND `the proceeding is a civil proceeding arising from having made the communication`

§§ `s 171 -- the audit committee`

-- (1) Subject to (2), a corporation described in s 102(2) shall, and any other corporation may, have an audit committee of not less
-- than three directors, a majority of whom are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates. (s 102(2) is out
-- of range: section 102.) The Director's authorization under (2) lifts the duty.
-- src:2066 | 171 (1) Subject to subsection (2), a corporation described in subsection 102(2) shall, and any other corporation may, have an audit committee composed of not less than three directors of the corporation, a majority of whom are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates.
@ref CBCA s 171(1) (src:2066)
GIVEN `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has authorized the corporation to dispense with an audit committee under subsection 171(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the corporation must have an audit committee within s 171(1)` MEANS
        `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)`
    AND (NOT `the Director has authorized the corporation to dispense with an audit committee under subsection 171(2)`)

@ref CBCA s 171(1) (src:2066)
GIVEN `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a corporation not described in subsection 102(2) may have an audit committee within s 171(1)` MEANS
    (NOT `the corporation is one described in subsection 102(2)`)

@ref CBCA s 171(1) (src:2066)
GIVEN `the number of members of the audit committee` IS A NUMBER
      `all the members are directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members who are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the audit committee is composed as s 171(1) requires within s 171(1)` MEANS
        `the number of members of the audit committee` AT LEAST 3
    AND `all the members are directors of the corporation`
    AND 2 TIMES `the number of members who are not officers or employees of the corporation or any of its affiliates` GREATER THAN `the number of members of the audit committee`

-- (2) The Director may, on the application of a corporation, authorize it to dispense with an audit committee, and may, if satisfied
-- that the shareholders will not be prejudiced, permit it to dispense with one on any reasonable conditions the Director thinks fit.
-- Whether the Director does is the Director's discretion and is not decided: the rules say when each power is open.
-- src:2068 | (2) The Director may, on the application of a corporation, authorize the corporation to dispense with an audit committee, and the Director may, if satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced, permit the corporation to dispense with an audit committee on any reasonable conditions that the Director thinks fit.
@ref CBCA s 171(2) (src:2068)
GIVEN `the corporation applies to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may authorize the corporation to dispense with an audit committee within s 171(2)` MEANS
    `the corporation applies to the Director`

@ref CBCA s 171(2) (src:2068)
GIVEN `the corporation applies to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Director may permit the corporation to dispense with an audit committee on conditions within s 171(2)` MEANS
        `the corporation applies to the Director`
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the shareholders will not be prejudiced`

-- (3) An audit committee shall review the financial statements before they are approved under s 158. The review is before the
-- approval if its date is on or before the approval's date: a date carries no time of day (fork F-171-before).
-- src:2070 | (3) An audit committee shall review the financial statements of the corporation before such financial statements are approved under section 158.
@ref CBCA s 171(3) (src:2070)
GIVEN `the date the audit committee reviewed the financial statements` IS A DATE
      `the date the financial statements were approved under section 158` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the audit committee reviewed the statements before they were approved within s 171(3)` MEANS
    `the date the audit committee reviewed the financial statements` AT MOST `the date the financial statements were approved under section 158`

-- (4) The auditor is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of the audit committee and, at the expense of the corporation,
-- to attend and be heard; and, if so requested by a member, shall attend every meeting held during the auditor's term of office.
-- src:2072 | (4) The auditor of a corporation is entitled to receive notice of every meeting of the audit committee and, at the expense of the corporation, to attend and be heard thereat; and, if so requested by a member of the audit committee, shall attend every meeting of the committee held during the term of office of the auditor.
@ref CBCA s 171(4) (src:2072)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor is entitled to notice of and to attend and be heard at the committee's meetings within s 171(4)` MEANS
    `the person is the auditor of the corporation`

@ref CBCA s 171(4) (src:2072)
GIVEN `a member of the audit committee has requested the auditor to attend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held during the term of office of the auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor must attend the committee's meeting within s 171(4)` MEANS
        `a member of the audit committee has requested the auditor to attend`
    AND `the meeting is held during the term of office of the auditor`

-- (5) The auditor or a member of the audit committee may call a meeting of the committee.
-- src:2074 | (5) The auditor of a corporation or a member of the audit committee may call a meeting of the committee.
@ref CBCA s 171(5) (src:2074)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a person may call a meeting of the audit committee within s 171(5)` MEANS
        `the person is the auditor of the corporation`
    OR  `the person is a member of the audit committee`

-- (6) A director or an officer shall forthwith notify the audit committee and the auditor of any error or mis-statement of which they
-- become aware in a financial statement the auditor or a former auditor has reported on. The relation: the committee and the auditor
-- hold the claim; the director or officer the duty.
-- src:2076 | (6) A director or an officer of a corporation shall forthwith notify the audit committee and the auditor of any error or mis-statement of which the director or officer becomes aware in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on.
@ref CBCA s 171(6) (src:2076)
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the director or officer must notify the committee and the auditor within s 171(6)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation`
    AND `the person becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement that the auditor or a former auditor has reported on`

@ref CBCA s 171(6) (src:2076)
GIVEN `the director or officer must notify the committee and the auditor within s 171(6)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person notified the audit committee forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person notified the auditor forthwith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty to notify the committee and the auditor is met within s 171(6)` MEANS
        (NOT `the director or officer must notify the committee and the auditor within s 171(6)`)
    OR  (    `the person notified the audit committee forthwith`
         AND `the person notified the auditor forthwith`)

-- (7) An auditor or former auditor who is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which
-- they have reported, if in their opinion it is material, shall inform each director.
-- src:2078 | (7) An auditor or former auditor of a corporation who is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported, if in their opinion the error or mis-statement is material, shall inform each director accordingly.
@ref CBCA s 171(7) (src:2078)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the opinion of the person the error or mis-statement is material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the auditor or former auditor must inform each director within s 171(7)` MEANS
        `the person is the auditor or a former auditor of the corporation`
    AND `the person is notified or becomes aware of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement on which they have reported`
    AND `in the opinion of the person the error or mis-statement is material`

-- (8) When the auditor informs the directors under (7), the directors shall (a) prepare and issue revised financial statements; or
-- (b) otherwise inform the shareholders and, if the corporation is required to comply with s 160, inform the Director in the same
-- manner as it informs the shareholders.
-- src:2080 | (8) When under subsection (7) the auditor or former auditor informs the directors of an error or mis-statement in a financial statement, the directors shall
-- src:2081 | (a) prepare and issue revised financial statements; or
-- src:2082 | (b) otherwise inform the shareholders and, if the corporation is one that is required to comply with section 160, it shall inform the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informs the shareholders.
@ref CBCA s 171(8) (src:2080-2082)
GIVEN `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the directors must act on the error or mis-statement within s 171(8)` MEANS
    `the auditor or former auditor informed the directors of an error or mis-statement under subsection 171(7)`

@ref CBCA s 171(8) (src:2080-2082)
GIVEN `the directors must act on the error or mis-statement within s 171(8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors prepared and issued revised financial statements` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors otherwise informed the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation is required to comply with section 160` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corporation informed the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informed the shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the duty of the directors is met within s 171(8)` MEANS
        (NOT `the directors must act on the error or mis-statement within s 171(8)`)
    OR  `the directors prepared and issued revised financial statements`
    OR  (    `the directors otherwise informed the shareholders`
         AND (    (NOT `the corporation is required to comply with section 160`)
              OR  `the corporation informed the Director of the error or mis-statement in the same manner as it informed the shareholders`))

-- (9) Every director or officer who knowingly fails to comply with (6) or (8) is guilty of an offence: fine not exceeding $5,000 or
-- imprisonment not exceeding six months, or both.
-- src:2084 | (9) Every director or officer of a corporation who knowingly fails to comply with subsection (6) or (8) is guilty of an offence and liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding five thousand dollars or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to both.
@ref CBCA s 171(9) (src:2084)
GIVEN `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person failed to comply with subsection 171(6) or (8)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knew that they failed to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a director or officer is guilty of an offence within s 171(9)` MEANS
        `the person is a director or an officer of the corporation`
    AND `the person failed to comply with subsection 171(6) or (8)`
    AND `the person knew that they failed to comply`

@ref CBCA s 171(9) (src:2084)
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV`
`the penalty ceiling within s 171(9)` MEANS
    `Penalty ceiling in Parts XI to XIV` WITH `maximum fine in dollars` IS 5000, `maximum imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

§§ `s 172 -- qualified privilege`

-- Any oral or written statement or report made under the Act by the auditor or a former auditor has qualified privilege.
-- src:2086 | 172 Any oral or written statement or report made under this Act by the auditor or former auditor of a corporation has qualified privilege.
@ref CBCA s 172 (src:2086)
GIVEN `it is an oral or written statement or report made under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the statement or report has qualified privilege within s 172` MEANS
        `it is an oral or written statement or report made under this Act`
    AND `it is made by the auditor or a former auditor of a corporation`
